{
  "id": "addisons",
  "name": "Addison's",
  "source": "John Sheeles (1688-1761), first printed c. 1720; the tune Joseph Addison's 'The spacious firmament on high' has carried since, called ADDISON'S in English hymnals and LONDON (Sheeles) in Hymnary. Melody transcribed from an ABC of the setting composite from A Hymnal (Episcopal), 1916 and Hymns Ancient and Modern, 1922, and checked against the Hymnary incipit for LONDON (Sheeles), 13325 43212 51232, which matches exactly. Public domain. NOT the Haydn tune CREATION, which carries the same text in American hymnals; see the note in docs/design/09-music.md.",
